><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Very high energy (high speed trauma + gross contamination)</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4</td></tr><tr><td colspan="2" align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1"><bold>Limb ischemia</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Pulse reduced or absent but perfusion normal</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-vhrm-6-1103">a</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Pulseless; paresthesias, diminished capillary refill</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-vhrm-6-1103">a</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Cool, paralyzed, insensate, numb</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-vhrm-6-1103">a</xref></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2" align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1"><bold>Shock</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Systolic BP always &#x0003e;90 mmHg</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Hypotensive transiently</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Persistent hypotension</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Age (years)</bold></td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;30</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">30&#x02013;50</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1</td